# Sequelize's query generator splices an attributes-array string straight into
# the SELECT when that string carries parentheses, because quoteIdentifier is
# skipped for exactly those strings (SQL injection, CWE-89; GHSA-f598-mfpv-gmfx,
# CVSS 10.0, fixed in 6.29.0). escapeAttributes in
# src/dialects/abstract/query-generator.js runs, at the vulnerable revision,
#
#   } else if (!attr[0].includes('(') && !attr[0].includes(')')) {
#     attr[0] = this.quoteIdentifier(attr[0]);
#   } else {
#     deprecations.noRawAttributes();
#   }
#
# so the else branch emits the attribute verbatim and only deprecates it, and
# the join two statements below splices attr[0] into the query text. The fixing
# commit d3f5b5a65e (the pool row's nocommit flag reflects advisory-side
# absence -- the commit resolves, reads in full, and names the CVE in its
# message and its error text) quotes the attribute when attributeBehavior is
# 'escape' and otherwise throws, unless the application opts into
# 'unsafe-legacy', which keeps the raw splice with the deprecation removed.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked: ORM-boundary SQL assembly, the identifier-position
# member of the settled family of ranks 1545, 1551, 1555, 1564, 1568, 1571,
# 1579 and 1602. The defect sits inside the library's own query assembly, and
# every file the fix touches is library source or a test
# (query-generator.js, sequelize.js, sequelize.d.ts, utils/deprecations.ts and
# six test files), so no application-level file differs between the two
# revisions: an application calling User.findAll({ attributes: [[col, 'value']] })
# is byte-identical before and after the upgrade, and a binding on that call
# site can never separate the revisions however it is written.
#
# Re-measured over three --cache off runs per revision on the real src/ tree
# (144 files, `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB`):
# 213/213/213 findings at 53bd9b7 (the fix's parent) and 213/213/213 at
# d3f5b5a65e, with identical per-rule tables on both sides (89 VYQL-INJ-001,
# 53 VYQL-INJ-013, 32 VYQL-INJ-134, 7 VYQL-CRY-006, 6 VYQL-INJ-011,
# 5 VYQL-INJ-008, 5 VYQL-DOS-001, 5 VYQL-CFG-014, 4 VYQL-INJ-009,
# 4 VYQL-AUTH-079, 2 VYQL-INJ-012, 1 VYQL-INJ-106) and the only textual
# differences eleven line-number shifts from the inserted throw block. The
# `-flags only` view agrees: 47 flags on each side with identical key sets,
# and the single query-generator flag is a code.SecretComparisonReview at
# dialects/oracle/query-generator.js:37, unrelated to the splice. Nothing
# reports anywhere in escapeAttributes (lines 1508-1545 at the parent,
# 1508-1558 at the fix); the nearest findings sit at 1342 and 1613.
#
# Diagnosis re-run on the request-driven shape: `match` labels req.query.col as
# code.HttpInput and puts no sink at all on the findAll call -- the only
# code.SqlExecution in the file is args[0] of router.get, a constant route
# string picked up by the method-name-wide sqlExecution673. `trace` from
# code.HttpInput dead-ends at res.json, and `resolve` leaves router.get,
# res.json and module.exports unresolved. So the miss is a missing sink
# binding, not a broken path: nothing labels a model query call as a query
# sink. The inversion the first pass recorded also survives -- the documented
# raw-SQL opt-in sequelize.literal(col) reports VYQL-INJ-001 today through
# sqlExecution137, while the request-driven attributes shape reports nothing,
# and the parameterized-where form stays clean.
#
# Later-shipped vocabulary checked and ruled out. The tree's only sequelize
# sink is sqlExecution18/sqlExecution138 on `sequelize.query` at args[0];
# findAll, findOne and findAndCountAll appear in no JavaScript binding at all
# (the nearest are the NoSQL sinks nosqlQuery464-466 on `Model.find`,
# `Model.findOne` and `Model.where`). The generic identifier-interpolation
# concept that did land, code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
# (VYQL-INJ-152), is emitted only from Go and Python bindings keyed on
# application-side shapes, and its documented neutraliser set -- allowlist
# membership or a driver identifier quoter -- cannot separate these revisions
# either, because this.quoteIdentifier is present in both. Two JavaScript
# SqlParameterization credits now exist (sqlstring.escape,
# pg-promise.parameterized), but both are explicit escape calls at the call
# site; neither credits an ORM's implicit parameterization of a where clause,
# which is what a sink on the model query would need to stay suppressible.
#
# The library-side discriminator that does separate the revisions fails the
# genericity test. In the IR the quoting call this.quoteIdentifier sits in the
# paren-free branch and the unquoted else branch holds exactly one call,
# deprecations.noRawAttributes(); the join that emits the attribute is
# byte-identical in both revisions. The only fact that distinguishes them is
# what the else branch does -- deprecate versus throw -- which is the fixing
# commit's own layout, and a binding keyed on it reports the same weakness
# written with any other non-throwing action. The two attr[].includes tests
# additionally carry vyql.internal.NeutralizerAssumption, so any clause keyed
# on the character test reads as validation rather than as the bypass.
#
# Closing this needs ORM query-position vocabulary -- which option positions of
# a model query are interpolated into SQL text rather than bound, with a
# JavaScript credit for the implicit parameterization of the rest -- and that
# is a weakness-class addition, not a localized construct. No ENGINE-GAPS.md
# entry and no definition change.
#
# Spec cve_rank1723 records the raw splice, the quoting-or-throwing form, the
# request-driven shape and the parameterized-where form, all asserting reject
# VYQL-INJ-001: when ORM query-position vocabulary lands, the raw-splice and
# request-driven forms must flip to expect while the parameterized-where form
# must keep rejecting.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, all four forms rejected.

test "rank1723: a parenthesis-carrying attribute is spliced raw into the SELECT"
  lang javascript
  file src/dialects/abstract/query-generator.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  escapeAttributes(attributes, options, mainTableAs) {
    return attributes && attributes.map(attr => {
      if (attr instanceof Utils.SequelizeMethod) {
        return this.handleSequelizeMethod(attr);
      }
      if (Array.isArray(attr)) {
        attr = attr.slice();

        if (attr[0] instanceof Utils.SequelizeMethod) {
          attr[0] = this.handleSequelizeMethod(attr[0]);
        } else if (!attr[0].includes('(') && !attr[0].includes(')')) {
          attr[0] = this.quoteIdentifier(attr[0]);
        } else {
          deprecations.noRawAttributes();
        }

        let alias = attr[1];

        if (this.options.minifyAliases) {
          alias = this._getMinifiedAlias(alias, mainTableAs, options);
        }

        attr = [attr[0], this.quoteIdentifier(alias)].join(' AS ');
      }

      return attr;
    });
  }
  ```

test "rank1723: the fixed revision quotes or throws instead of emitting the attribute verbatim"
  lang javascript
  file src/dialects/abstract/query-generator.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  escapeAttributes(attributes, options, mainTableAs) {
    return attributes && attributes.map(attr => {
      if (attr instanceof Utils.SequelizeMethod) {
        return this.handleSequelizeMethod(attr);
      }
      if (Array.isArray(attr)) {
        attr = attr.slice();

        if (attr[0] instanceof Utils.SequelizeMethod) {
          attr[0] = this.handleSequelizeMethod(attr[0]);
        } else if (this.options.attributeBehavior === 'escape' || !attr[0].includes('(') && !attr[0].includes(')')) {
          attr[0] = this.quoteIdentifier(attr[0]);
        } else if (this.options.attributeBehavior !== 'unsafe-legacy') {
          throw new Error('Attributes cannot include parentheses: wrap the attribute in a literal() call, or set the attributeBehavior option.');
        }

        let alias = attr[1];

        if (this.options.minifyAliases) {
          alias = this._getMinifiedAlias(alias, mainTableAs, options);
        }

        attr = [attr[0], this.quoteIdentifier(alias)].join(' AS ');
      }

      return attr;
    });
  }
  ```

test "rank1723: a request-supplied column reaches the attributes array of a model query"
  lang javascript
  file routes/users.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  const express = require('express');
  const router = express.Router();

  router.get('/rows', async (req, res) => {
    const col = req.query.col;
    const rows = await User.findAll({ attributes: [[col, 'value']] });
    res.json(rows);
  });

  module.exports = router;
  ```

test "rank1723: constant attributes and a parameterized where stay clean"
  lang javascript
  file routes/users.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  const express = require('express');
  const router = express.Router();

  router.get('/rows', async (req, res) => {
    const rows = await User.findAll({ attributes: [['id', 'value']], where: { id: req.query.id } });
    res.json(rows);
  });

  module.exports = router;
  ```
